From 9c01735e2d3261eb705382d367db776c666df01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:24:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Decomposition: M 20 1 chooses the partition automatically, M
 20 2 and 5 retired

M 20 1 (the default) now picks the layout mx x my x mz and the cut planes by the load:
of all layouts of the M 10 ranks (in the directions M 11-13 allow, at least 3 cells per
subdomain) the one with the lightest heaviest subdomain, the cuts placed so that the
heaviest subdomain is as light as possible, and among the layouts within 1 % of it the
one with the least cut area. It replaces the layout of before (least cut area, equal
widths) only when its heaviest subdomain is at least 5 % lighter, so grids without a
load imbalance keep their partition.

The work of a cell is 1 for an active cell and 0 for a solid one. For the column models
of REEF3D (A 10 2, 3, 5 in ctrl.txt of the case folder) it is the work of the water
columns: 1 per column, 0.1 for a dry column (geodat bed at or above F 60 of ctrl.txt, or
no active cell).

Retired: M 20 2 (analyse/correction) and M 20 5 (weighted) run as M 20 1, with a
message. M 21, M 34, M 35, M 41, M 45 are ignored with a message. M 20 3 and 4 are
unchanged.

REEF3D M 40 decomposes the global grid file with the same code (dmpart), so the
subdomains are identical.

Architect: Hans Bihs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NGQcgqpqSqLZ42oy1GcuZL
